-strings\", \"concept\": \".NET assembly bytes inside a script (Assembly.Load / Add-Type -Path / embedded resource): read the plan from metadata heaps\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Base id D19 = `managed-assembly-bridge`; the obvious escalation is real managed bytes. dotnet_strings(data)->{us: [..], strings: [..], resources: {name: bytes}, typedefs, methods}: locate the PE (pefile allowed) or raw `BSJB` metadata root, walk streams `#~`/`#Strings`/`#US` (compressed-length-prefixed UTF-16LE user strings)/`#Blob`, ManifestResource rows + the .resources blob (`CEFAEDFE` ResourceReader magic), Costura `costura.*.dll.compressed` (raw deflate). Carrier discovery: base64 `TVqQ`/`TVpQ` (MZ), hex `4d5a90`, int arrays `77,90,144`, gzip `H4sI` of an MZ, inside PS `[Reflection.Assembly]::Load([Convert]::FromBase64String(..))`, C# `Assembly.Load(byte[])`, `Add-Type -Path`. Then run v3_plan / find_codecs over every user string + resource. ilspycmd (INSTALLED) is the oracle only. Gate: synthetic minimal metadata blobs built in the fixture (no compiler), D1-D19 members classify as non-assembly.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"managed-bridge-hosts\", \"concept\": \".NET-hosted script surfaces beyond ASPX/MSBuild: PS Add-Type C#, InstallUtil/RegAsm/RegSvcs, ashx/asmx/cshtml, classic ASP, Workflow Compiler XOML\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 host_profile spelling `aspx_inline_csharp` (<container>_<inline>_<lang>). managed_host(name, src)->{profile_guess, lang, inner_texts}: PowerShell `Add-Type -TypeDefinition @\\\"..\\\"@ [-Language CSharp]` / `-MemberDefinition` / `CSharpCodeProvider.CompileAssemblyFromSource(` / `[ScriptBlock]::Create`; `.ashx`/`.asmx` `<%@ WebHandler|WebService Language=\\\"C#\\\" Class=..%>` + code; Razor `.cshtml` `@{ .. }`/`@functions{ }`; classic ASP `<%@ Language=VBScript %>` `<% %>` and `<script language=\\\"JScript\\\" runat=\\\"server\\\">`; `[RunInstaller(true)]` Installer.Uninstall / `[ComRegisterFunction]`; Microsoft.Workflow.Compiler XOML `<x:Code><![CDATA[..]]>`; `csc.exe /out` invoked from batch with the source in an echo-redirected file. Extract each inner text (via nested-string-carrier-unescape), route to the language reader, report the host profile guess. Gate: D19 ASPX + D14 MSBuild + D8 php_webshell still route identically.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"solver-lib-v3-fallback\", \"concept\": \"carried solve.py must ask lib.codec.v3_plan when its own v=3 read yields nothing\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19: lib.codec.v3_plan already decoded the ASPX escaped-nested carrier, but the carried solve.py `_v3` only used its own V3_MARK/descriptor regexes, so 11 ids went planless and the race harness probed guesses. The D20 solver-authoring pass: in analyse_v3, if no candidate peels to `v=`, call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) (and lib.codec.find_codecs) before giving up; log which reader won. Same for D18 SPLIT (now in both).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"evidence-type-router\", \"concept\": \"classify any NON-script member (second evidence type) and dispatch to its reader\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D17 prompt named network evidence, D18 native process telemetry; neither shipped yet, but the day it does the worker must know in one call what the extra file is. evidence_kind(name, bytes)->{kind: pcap|pcapng|har|zeek|sysmon_evtx|sysmon_xml|sysmon_json|security_4688|auditd|ps_listing|procmon_csv|w3c|squid|edr_json|unknown, reader: lib function name, records: n} by magic/shape (ElfFile header for EVTX, `<Events>`/`<Event xmlns=` XML, JSON lines with EventID/ProcessGuid/event.code, `type=SYSCALL`, `UID PID PPID C STIME`, `\\\"Time of Day\\\",\\\"Process Name\\\",\\\"PID\\\"` Procmon CSV). Then route: network -> network_indicators, process -> process_events (gap process-telemetry-windows/-linux-text), file/registry -> file_registry_events. Gate: every D1-D18 script member classifies as `script` (no false positives). Attempt 1 failed (D18 night): retry, smaller scope first (magic/shape classifier + reader name only), D18 process readers now exist to route to.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"file-registry-telemetry-reconcile\", \"concept\": \"declared file/registry/schedule indicators vs file/registry/task telemetry\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The daily second-evidence rotation went network (D17) -> process (D18); file and registry are the obvious next. file_registry_events(data)->[{ts, kind: file_create|file_delete|reg_set|reg_create|task_create|service_install, path, value, details, image, pid}] from Sysmon EID 11/23/26 (TargetFilename), 12/13/14 (TargetObject, Details), Security 4698/4702 (TaskContent XML), System 7045 (ServiceName/ImagePath), auditd PATH records, MFT/USN CSV text. reconcile_artifacts(plans, events) compares plan file_path/next_stage/cron_path/schedule_path/service_name/registry keys (canon: HKLM\\\\ vs HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\\\ vs \\\\REGISTRY\\\\MACHINE\\\\, case-insensitive Windows paths, %APPDATA% expansion) -> declared_only/observed_only/both + an answer helper like reconcile_answer. Attempt 1 failed (D18 night): retry with Sysmon 11/12/13 + 4698 only first, then auditd/USN.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"csharp-literal-fold\", \"concept\": \"static folding of assembled C#/.NET strings (descriptor built at runtime instead of a literal)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"If a C#/VB.NET/F# variant assembles the descriptor: fold `string.Concat(..)`, `string.Join(\\\"\\\", new[] {..})`, `new string(new char[] {'v','=',..})`, `(char)0x76`/`(char)118`, `Encoding.UTF8|ASCII|Unicode.GetString(new byte[] {..})`, `Convert.FromBase64String`, `Convert.FromHexString`, `BitConverter`, `StringBuilder().Append(..)` chains, `$\\\"{a}{b}\\\"` over const locals, `.Reverse()`/`Array.Reverse`, `ToCharArray()` + `^ key` loops with literal keys, `\\\\u0076` escapes, verbatim/raw strings; VB `ChrW(118) & ..`, F# `String.concat \\\"\\\" [..]`. Pure regex/const-propagation over literals (no ast module, no compiler). Gate: D19 csx plans re-assembled in each form fold back to the same plan.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"fsharp-vbnet-script-route\", \"concept\": \"F# .fsx and VB.NET .vb / .vbx v=3 polyglots (next .NET languages)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Make sure the generic marker/descriptor readers cover: F# `// ` and `(* HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:.. *)` comments, `let descriptor_<id> = \\\"..\\\"`, triple-quoted `\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"`, `[<Literal>]` consts, `Map.ofList [ \\\"descriptor\\\", descriptor_<id> ]`; VB.NET `' HUNTRESS..` / `REM` comments, `Dim|Const descriptor_<id> As String = \\\"..\\\"` with `\\\"\\\"` escapes and `& _` line continuations, `New Dictionary(Of String, String) From {{\\\"descriptor\\\", ..}}`; JScript.NET `import System;` `var descriptor_<id> : String = \\\"..\\\"`. Family guesses `polyglot-fsharp_script` / `polyglot-vb_net` / `polyglot-jscript_net`. Gate: fixture battery of D19 plans in each syntax.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"handoff-chain-resolve\", \"concept\": \"corpus-level handoff graph: where each bridge 'actually leads' (next_language -> member -> terminal)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 prompt 'resolve each static handoff and work out where the bridge actually leads' was answered by per-file next-language ids, but a corpus-level question (terminal language, chain length, which member a handoff resolves to, cycles, the file whose declared next_language disagrees with its code's spawn/write target) is the natural escalation. handoff_graph(plans_by_member, sources=None)->{edges: [(member, next_language, resolved_members)], chains, terminals, cycles, mismatches}; resolve next_language to members by plan language= / file family (`polyglot-<lang>-*`, host files, legacy v=1/v=2 names: jscript->.js, vbscript->.vbs, batch->.bat/.cmd, powershell->.ps1, python->.py, bash->.sh, node->.mjs); code-side target from declared_spawns/fetch_sites. handoff_answer(g, kind, accepted_values, what=). Reuse download_graph internals.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jvm-script-host-route\", \"concept\": \"JSP webshell / Groovy / Java single-file / Nashorn hosts\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Sibling of D8 php_webshell and D19 aspx_inline_csharp on the JVM side: `<%@ page language=\\\"java\\\" import=..%>`, `<%-- HUNTRESS.. --%>` comments, scriptlets `<% %>`/declarations `<%! %>`, `Runtime.getRuntime().exec`/`ProcessBuilder`; Groovy `def descriptor_x = '..'` / `\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"` / `'''..'''`, `.execute()`, `.decodeBase64()`; Java `static final String DESCRIPTOR_X = \\\"..\\\";` with `\\\\uXXXX` escapes processed BEFORE lexing (unicode-escaped `\\\\u0022` can close a string or hide a comment end); Nashorn/Rhino `jrunscript -e`. Readers via nested-string-carrier-unescape; profile guesses `jsp_scriptlet`/`groovy_jenkins`. Gate: fixture battery.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx (and future .tcl .r .groovy .kts .go .rs .awk .yml .tf .xsl .reg .inf). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml). D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..). D18: `polyglot-google_apps_script` (campaign GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT-, url host google_apps_script-..) while its host file is hyphenated `host-google-docs-sidebar-google-apps-script` (profile google_docs_sidebar). D19: `polyglot-csharp_script` (campaign CSHARP_SCRIPT-, url host csharp_script-..) and host `host-aspx-inline-csharp-csharp-script` (profile aspx_inline_csharp, file extension .csx although the bytes are an ASPX page).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D19 shipped .csx source only (static read was enough). Install dotnet-script only if a csx variant needs `#load`/`#r` resolution: dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script (parse only; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild/Assembly.Load payloads).\"}\n]\n```\n","numLines":46,"startLine":180,"totalLines":225}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017jSipxauo3UZPDwA7ssVeQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
