{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDZ4rt5NG991PcnaTnrg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017KmSXVoNTxF3YR92w76TUN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/script-analysis.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1, a[:70]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"# script-analysis — coverage atlas (D1-D19 seen vs. D20+ candidates)\",\"# script-analysis — coverage atlas (D1-D20 seen vs. D21+ candidates)\")\ni=s.index(\"Updated 2026-10-19\"); j=s.index(\"Read with `reference/techniques\")\ns=s[:i]+\"\"\"Updated 2026-10-20 after D20 (1329 ids, 145 members; D20 \"The Butler Did It\" / base `jenkins-pipeline-intrusion` added\nGroovy `.groovy` + a `jenkins_pipeline` host AND a `classic_asp` host for the OLD language VBScript (`.vbs` file holding an ASP\npage) + 2 Bash; all plain one-line v=3 carriers, no twist; single CORRECT T+13 s 0 wrong, TT 5.0 s, Mastery 11.9 s first try).\nEvery D19-night gap is built except evidence-type-router / file-registry-telemetry-reconcile (given up, 2 attempts each), so\nthe queue below is rebuilt from the D20 direction (CI/build hosts, JVM languages, hosts for prior languages). \"\"\"+s[j:]\nrep(\"\"\"  `\\\\\"`-quoted (lib.codec.v3_plan handles it; the carried solve.py needed a patch). The real D20+ risk\"\"\",\"\"\"  `\\\\\"`-quoted (lib.codec.v3_plan handles it; the carried solve.py needed a patch). D20 had no carrier twist. The real D21+ risk\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  aspx_inline_csharp (D19: web-page host, file still named `.csx`).\"\"\",\"\"\"  aspx_inline_csharp (D19: web-page host, file still named `.csx`), jenkins_pipeline + classic_asp (D20; classic_asp wraps\n  VBScript = first host for a PRIOR language, first day with two host files).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"C# script + ASPX inline host; base id `managed-assembly-bridge`, prompt \"a bridge that carries managed code back into the\n  script